WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:42.060
Exilag and other Jewish dignitaries.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:50.880
You see, according to rabbinic historiography, after the initial two millennia of chaos,

00:00:50.880 --> 00:01:02.080
Abraham ushered a new era, the era of Torah, which ended 2,000 years later, about the year

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:12.760
240 of the coming era, the time when the famous Talmudic Academy of Surah was founded, not

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:17.040
too far away from Abraham's original home.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:34.200
It was a fit occasion to open the new academic year and to greet the students that had come from near and far away places to continue Abraham's journey.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.500
What is the meaning of that journey?

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:52.660
The term, and they went forth describing Abraham and Sarah's departure from Mesopotamia, is

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:56.340
particularly significant.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:09.460
This term not only means to go, to depart, but also to be liberated, to go forth in freedom.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:18.020
It is the same term usually translated as Exodus describing Israel's departure from

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:22.460
the house of bondage in Egypt.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:29.780
In the context of our story, it means that Abraham and Sarah, when well advanced in years

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:40.840
, broke away from the system of values enslaving them and started

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:49.460
a new life, a life that rejuvenated them both spiritually and biologically.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:54.720
Abraham lived 100 years more, and Sarah 62.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.600
Indeed, about a thousand years later,

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:04.400
when the people of Israel were in material and spiritual decline,

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:08.620
Isaiah calls forth the figures of Abraham and Sarah

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.400
to inspire them to overcome their despair.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:16.180
Look into the rock from where you were hewn,

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.300
and to the pit from where you were digged.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:27.460
Look into Abraham your father and into Sarah that bare you, for he was alone when I called

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.460
him.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:39.060
And I blessed him, that is spiritually, and increased him, that is materially.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:46.940
In order to grasp Abraham's spiritual bondage, it will be necessary to consider some of the

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:53.940
the essential features of Mesopotamian civilization. Since early antiquity, there were two dominant

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:05.100
civilizations flourishing, one in Egypt and the other in Mesopotamia, with totally different

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:15.360
philosophies of man and society. Mesopotamia rejected the idea of one and the other as

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:28.060
single omnipotent God. Individually, the gods of the Babylonian pantheon held only limited power.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:39.460
Ultimate power resided in the totality of the gods. It was the effect of different configurations

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:48.160
and alliances established by the gods and therefore subject to manipulation.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:59.800
These alliances were revised every year, giving rise to new configurations of power and ideologies.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:06.200
This concept of religion was a replica of the political system.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:12.360
The Mesopotamian king did not represent absolute power.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:19.500
The authority of the king was limited by the power of the gods above and the consensus

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:27.160
of the elders below to whom he was accountable.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:36.460
They also conceived of a cosmic and impersonal law called Kitum, to which even the king was

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:39.340
its humble servant.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:46.800
In this way, the rights of the individual were protected and the abuses of authority

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.920
checked.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:06:00.800
In many significant aspects, the Mesopotamian society resembled our own modern society in

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:01.460
the West.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:10.300
Scholars have pointed out our debt to Mesopotamian civilization, particularly in the fields of

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:10.860
government.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:14.920
Democracy seems to have been a Mesopotamian invention.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:17.180
Law and science.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:26.720
Perhaps this is why it is so easy for us to understand the frustration of a 75-year-old

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:36.900
man at the twilight of his life with the melodies of a society that produces spiritual anarchy,

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:43.700
intellectual relativism, social apathy and bewilderment.

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:48.100
A distinguished ancient Near Eastern scholar observed,

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:57.880
The collapse of Nineveh and Babylon was due not so much to the superiority of outside

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:06.460
powers as to the crushing weight of the internal structure.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:14.820
The Tower of Babel is the symbol of a society without absolutes.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:22.980
It represents the society in which genuine human communication is excluded.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:32.880
The individual is condemned to existential solitude, deafened by the tumult of languages

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:36.760
he cannot possibly understand.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:58.760
It is the most difficult thing to do.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:09.760
society and goes searching for the promised land? In his journey away from Mesopotamia,

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:19.760
Abraham is stretching his hand to everyone who can feel the anguish of an individual

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.260
without ultimate goals and aspirations.

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.220
Let us hold his hand

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:32.280
and follow his footsteps into the promised land.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:39.260
At the time of the Patriarchs,

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:43.660
the land of Canaan was a scarcely populated area

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:49.320
inhabited by people of Semitic and non-Semitic background.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:59.760
Both economically and culturally it was under the influence of Egypt.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:05.940
Eventually Abraham goes to Egypt.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:13.440
There he discovers the other great civilization of antiquity.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:22.960
many fundamental issues, it was diametrically opposed to Mesopotamia.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:32.780
To begin with, although Egypt was strongly polytheistic, it believed essentially in one

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:38.620
single power for the entire cosmos.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:44.860
This power was perpetually incarnated in the Pharaoh.

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:54.060
The Pharaoh was divine and a depository of absolute power.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:10:01.620
He was above all and accountable to none.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:09.020
In such a system, no laws or rights can be truly operative.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:19.500
As the great Egyptologist John A. Wilson remarked, the authority of codified law would have competed

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:24.720
with the personal authority of the pharaoh.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:33.280
The people of Egypt, regardless of their social status and economic positions, were mere slaves

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:35.620
of the monarch.

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:42.420
Their own bodies belonged to the Pharaoh.

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:53.720
This absolute power produced an absolute stable society, one that is unparalleled in the annals

00:10:53.720 --> 00:11:08.280
of history. As slaves of Pharaoh, the individuals had no rights, but they enjoyed absolute stability.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:20.140
In Egypt, time was static. There was no real past or future. Changes were superficial disturbances

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:30.640
of the established order. The present was overwhelming and irremovable. In a profound

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:46.780
sense, ancient Egypt is an excellent illustration of totalitarianism in its most developed form.

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:54.540
In the structure of Egyptian thought, monotheism is possible.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:12:06.120
Indeed, upon his return to the land of Canaan, Abraham met Melchizedek, the king and priest

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:15.480
of Shalem, who pronounced the first monotheistic formula in Biblical literature.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:24.960
He referred to God as the Most High God, Creator of heaven and earth.

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:35.740
Thereupon, Abraham adopted this formula and used it when giving an oath to the king of Sodom.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:40.800
This formula is highly significant.

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:48.560
As we shall see, it expresses Egyptian ideology.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:58.180
The term Kone that we translated Creator means also Possessor, Master.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:01.440
The meaning is clear.

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:11.300
God, as the Creator of the universe, is also its absolute master and possessor.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:19.120
Within the Egyptian culture prevailing in Canaan at that time, this means that God is

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:22.820
the Pharaoh of the universe.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:38.420
It seems that the only viable alternative to Mesopotamian relativism was Egyptian totalitarianism.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:47.280
It must have been a very sad moment when later into the day, Abraham realized the ultimate

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:55.520
implication of this doctrine. A doctrine that he first visualized in his youth and finally

00:13:55.520 --> 00:14:07.180
understood after a long journey in his old age. When God appeared to Abraham that night,

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:15.520
He began with the words, Al-Tira'a Abram, fear not, Abram.

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:25.900
Biblical commentators were puzzled with this assurance, as it implies that Abraham was afraid.

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:31.840
What could have alarmed Abraham, wonder the commentators?

00:14:31.840 --> 00:14:38.280
To my mind, the answer is quite obvious.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:46.660
Nothing could be more awesome and depressing than a pharaonic God ruling the universe.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:51.680
I am your shield, God continues.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:55.040
Your reward shall be very great.

00:14:56.400 --> 00:15:01.160
It was a totally new perception of God.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:12.400
I, like Pharaoh, the God of Abraham will be a shield to men and a source of reward and satisfaction.

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:26.800
According to this perception, it is not sufficient to ascertain that man ought to serve God, but also that God wants to serve man.

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:35.860
It is not surprising, therefore, to find Abraham turning to God with a question,

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:42.480
God Almighty, what can you give me?

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:50.480
Again, many commentators expressed discomfort with this question.

00:15:50.480 --> 00:15:59.920
In their minds, it was unacceptable that a great religious figure, let alone Abraham,

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:06.300
would ask from God, what can you do for me?

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:12.840
I do not agree with this view.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:20.080
The God of Abraham is not an aloof Pharaoh, high and unapproachable.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:21.080
Quite the contrary.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:30.460
If there is a single message that comes loud and clear throughout the scriptures is that

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:39.920
the Almighty Lord, sole creator of the entire cosmos of galaxies and everything that reigns

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:48.720
in His infinite perfection, has an infinite desire to be loved and bestow His boundless

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:59.540
goodness into all of us. From the pharaonic point of view, the question what can you do

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:11.120
for me is an abomination. From the point of view of our Torah, it is an act of faith,

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:14.700
an acknowledgement of God's infinite mercy and goodness.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.560
As a matter of fact,

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:21.860
at the end of that vision we are told,

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:25.940
and he, Abraham, believed in the Lord,

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:32.860
and he, God, counted to him for righteousness.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:36.160
As you know quite well,

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:40.420
the term tzedakah that we translated righteousness

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:44.600
actually means charity.

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:50.020
God perceived Abraham's trust in him

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:54.760
as an act of charity and loving kindness.

00:17:56.640 --> 00:18:00.140
How dissimilar is this God

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.660
from the God of Matisetic?

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:07.940
Let us continue with Abraham's vision.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:20.080
As we know, Abraham's request from God was to have a child, a request that implied biological rejuvenation.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:29.640
It is crucial to note, therefore, that before granting this request, God tells Abraham,

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:37.360
Look now towards heaven and count the stars, if you be able to count them.

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:43.660
And he said unto him, So shall your seed be.

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:56.200
The rabbis explained that Abraham still believed in astrology, a science for which Mesopotamia

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:58.200
is famous.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:05.900
Abraham, the rabbis continued, was convinced that the astrological configurations of the

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:12.560
stars had determined that he will be childless.

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:21.060
The rabbis ascertained that God lifted Abraham above the heavenly canopy from where he could

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:32.000
view the entire array of the stars and told him, go away from your astrological beliefs.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:43.620
It is worth observing that the Hebrew TCHE is the same term that we explain to mean go

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:48.420
forth in freedom, be liberated.

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:53.460
The sense of the message is quite simple.

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:58.440
Abraham was still a prisoner of his cultural background.

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:05.120
He needed to make another step forward to finally attain freedom.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:14.340
But why was it necessary for God to lift Abraham above the celestial canopy

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:18.040
and then challenge him to count the stars?

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:22.800
Moreover, God's promise,

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:25.760
so shall your seed be,

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:28.400
seems impossible.

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:37.080
the number of the stars far exceeds the population that our planet Earth can support.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:49.480
I believe that the key to the code and message of this passage lies in the word Lyspor.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:55.320
This word that we translated to count

00:20:55.320 --> 00:21:00.340
is primarily an astrological term

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:04.640
and it has the sense of configuration

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:10.460
It means to count or calibrate something

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:13.120
within a definite frame or figure

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.520
Modern scholarship

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:23.520
particularly in the fields of linguistics and anthropology, have pointed out how the

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:30.700
culture in which one lives affects the sensory perception of the individual. What one hears

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:40.380
and sees is significantly determined by the culture in which one lives. We can easily

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:48.940
We can easily picture Abraham ever since his youth, lifting his eyes towards heaven and

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:57.940
actually seeing the ominous configurations of the stars announcing his impotence to the

00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:00.160
world.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:07.700
To change this perception, Abraham had to change his perspective.

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:18.120
This is why God lifted Abraham above the celestial canopy in order for him to gain a total perspective

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:20.680
of the stars.

00:22:20.680 --> 00:22:24.580
Can you lispor etako habim?

00:22:24.580 --> 00:22:31.780
Can you that is to perceive the stars in their astrological configuration as the Lord?

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:34.080
The answer is obvious.

00:22:34.080 --> 00:22:40.980
The patterns of perceptions imposed upon the individual by his culture become meaningless

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:44.700
from the total perspective.

00:22:44.700 --> 00:22:54.160
Then, and then alone, Abraham completed his journey from Mesopotamia and attained genuine

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:55.160
freedom.

00:22:55.160 --> 00:23:05.540
For the first time in his long life, Abraham saw the stars as they are, not according to

00:23:05.540 --> 00:23:12.040
some conventionalism controlling his inner perceptions.

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:21.400
He was still immersed in the new view of a universe without chains when God told him,

00:23:21.400 --> 00:23:24.880
so shall your seed be.

00:23:26.360 --> 00:23:32.200
It was an assurance that his posterity, like him,

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:36.720
will be able to ascend above particulars

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:41.140
and perceive reality from a total perspective.

00:23:41.740 --> 00:23:46.860
The children of Abraham may be enslaved and persecuted from without,

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:49.520
but not from within.

00:23:49.520 --> 00:23:53.200
Our Torah Make Us Free

00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:59.100
We are almost at the end of our sermon.

00:23:59.840 --> 00:24:05.360
We began with Abraham's journey away from cultural bondage into spiritual freedom.

00:24:05.880 --> 00:24:09.740
We considered the options open to the ancient man,

00:24:10.540 --> 00:24:15.660
that of Mesopotamian relativism or Egyptian totalitarianism.

00:24:15.660 --> 00:24:20.640
We also touched upon Abraham's vision of religious humanism

00:24:20.640 --> 00:24:25.420
A vision that was eventually fulfilled at the fault of Mount Sinai

00:24:25.420 --> 00:24:30.100
When God and the children of Israel established a buried covenant

00:24:30.100 --> 00:24:32.740
Determining the grounds of their relationship

00:24:32.740 --> 00:24:38.640
There is a final word

00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:42.420
Bearing on the character of Abraham's journey

00:24:42.420 --> 00:24:46.040
that I would like to share with you.

00:24:47.860 --> 00:24:52.200
The Sidra opens with God telling Abraham

00:24:52.200 --> 00:24:54.140
to leave his birthplace

00:24:54.140 --> 00:24:58.580
and go into the land that I will show you.

00:24:59.620 --> 00:25:02.260
El Ahareh Asher Areca.

00:25:03.760 --> 00:25:08.780
The Hebrew Areca has a double connotation.

00:25:08.780 --> 00:25:14.560
It means the land which I will show you.

00:25:15.620 --> 00:25:21.000
But it also means the land in which I shall show you,

00:25:21.780 --> 00:25:25.820
in the sense of displaying Abraham to the world.

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:34.240
Thus the peculiar character of Abraham's journey in our own history.

00:25:34.240 --> 00:25:44.240
On the one hand, God has showed us many lands throughout our long and painful history.

00:25:44.240 --> 00:25:51.240
We have learned much from these lands and we are grateful.

00:25:51.240 --> 00:26:02.240
But on the other hand, we were also displayed as something sacred and unique, a paradigm

00:26:02.240 --> 00:26:04.900
for mankind to emulate.

00:26:04.900 --> 00:26:18.900
As I look into this congregation and see Abraham's children pursuing that primeval journey, I

00:26:18.900 --> 00:26:23.120
cannot help feeling overwhelmed.

00:26:23.120 --> 00:26:25.140
God bless you all.

00:26:32.240 --> 00:27:02.220
Thank you.

00:27:02.240 --> 00:27:32.220
Thank you.

00:27:32.240 --> 00:28:02.220
Thank you.

00:28:02.240 --> 00:28:32.220
Thank you.

00:28:32.240 --> 00:29:02.220
Thank you.

00:29:02.240 --> 00:29:32.220
Thank you.

00:29:32.240 --> 00:30:02.220
Thank you.

00:30:02.240 --> 00:30:32.220
Thank you.

00:30:32.240 --> 00:31:02.220
Thank you.

00:31:02.240 --> 00:31:32.220
Thank you.

00:31:32.240 --> 00:32:02.220
Thank you.

00:32:02.240 --> 00:32:32.220
Thank you.

